Sample mod for the A316 modding build (tools/modbuild.py). Build it with

    $EXHUME/.venv/bin/python tools/modbuild.py --patch examples/mod-example/arm-version.patch --version 317 --out build/mod/example/ARMStore.bin

which copies src/ to build/mod/tree, applies this there (src/ is not changed) and builds
build/mod/example/ARMStore.bin with 317 in its header. It changes one thing that shows: HR21,
the ARM version the inverter reports on Modbus (meter.c's modbus_hr_update fills it with the
constant 0x13C, 316), says 317 (0x13D). The running ARM only takes an ARMStore.bin whose header
version differs from its own and has the same hundreds, so a mod needs a new version in the
header (--version) as well; HR21 then agrees with it.

0x13C is a Thumb-2 modified immediate (0x9E shifted left by 1) and 0x13D is not, so armcc loads the new value
with a 4-byte MOVW (f240 103d) where it had a 4-byte MOV.W (f44f 709e): the code stays the same
size and nothing moves.

--- a/src/app/comm/meter.c
+++ b/src/app/comm/meter.c
@@ -1111,7 +1111,7 @@
     hr_regs[18] = bms_fw_version;
     hr_regs[19] = dsp_version_hr19;
     hr_regs[HR_ENABLE_CHARGE_TARGET] = cfg_settings.enable_charge_target;
-    hr_regs[21] = 0x13c;
+    hr_regs[21] = 0x13d;     /* mod: HR21, the ARM version, says 317 */
     hr_regs[22] = usb_device_inserted;
     hr_regs[23] = peek_chip[0];
     hr_regs[24] = peek_addr;
